{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Observability · Fuzzphony{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h2>Observability</h2>
<p>Fuzzphony reports every search, sync and reindex operation through a <code>MetricsCollector</code>:
<code>NullMetricsCollector</code> (default, zero cost), <code>LoggingMetricsCollector</code> (structured
log lines, <code>debug</code> level, channel <code>fuzzphony</code>), or <code>PrometheusMetricsCollector</code>
for Prometheus and Grafana. The bundle picks the Prometheus one on its own when
<code>promphp/prometheus_client_php</code> is installed and <code>apcu</code> is loaded and enabled in that
process, and quietly falls back to logging otherwise &mdash; nothing breaks without them. This demo has
neither installed, so it runs the logging collector.</p>

<form method="get" class="searchbar" data-loading-message="Searching…">
    <input type="search" name="q" value="{{ query }}" aria-label="Query to measure" placeholder="Search the catalogue…">
    <button type="submit" class="primary">Search</button>
</form>
<div class="examples">
    {% for label, example in examples %}
        <a class="button" href="{{ path('observability', {q: example}) }}">{{ label }}: <code>{{ example }}</code></a>
    {% endfor %}
</div>

<h3>What this search reported</h3>
<p>Query: <code>{{ query }}</code> &middot; {{ total }} hits</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Kind</th><th>This run</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.search.took_ms</code></th><td>histogram</td><td>{{ took_ms }} ms</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.search.fallback</code></th><td>counter</td><td>{{ fallback ? '+1 (typo tolerance ran)' : 'not incremented (exact match was enough)' }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>SQL statements</th><td>&mdash;</td><td>{{ statements }}</td></tr>
        {% if queue %}
            <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.queue.depth</code></th><td>gauge</td><td>{{ queue.message }}</td></tr>
        {% endif %}
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>The log line for it</h3>
<pre><code>fuzzphony.metric {"event":"fuzzphony.search.took_ms","value":{{ took_ms }},"index":"catalog"}{% if fallback %}

fuzzphony.metric {"event":"fuzzphony.search.fallback","by":1,"index":"catalog"}{% endif %}</code></pre>
<p class="muted">The query text is left out of the line unless you opt in (<code>logQueryText</code>), and is never a
Prometheus label (one time series per distinct query would never stop growing).</p>

<h3>Everything Fuzzphony can report</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Kind</th><th>From</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.search.took_ms</code></th><td>histogram</td><td>every search</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.search.fallback</code></th><td>counter</td><td>searches that needed typo tolerance</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.&lt;operation&gt;.duration_ms</code> / <code>.errors</code></th><td>histogram / counter</td><td>every engine operation (rebuild, refresh, queue, pruning&hellip;)</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.queue.depth</code></th><td>gauge</td><td>the sync worker, once per cycle</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.queue.processed</code></th><td>counter</td><td>the sync worker</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.worker.rebuild_failures</code></th><td>counter</td><td>the sync worker</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fuzzphony.messenger.refresh.duration_ms</code> / <code>.errors</code></th><td>histogram / counter</td><td>the ORM-sync Messenger handler</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Prometheus and Grafana</h3>
<p>With the Prometheus collector these become scrapeable series (expose them with a small
<code>/metrics</code> route, see <code>docs/observability.md</code>), and
<code>docs/grafana/fuzzphony-overview.json</code> is a ready-made dashboard: search latency and
fallback rate, queue depth, errors by operation, and the sync handler. Import it under
Dashboards &rarr; New &rarr; Import. <code>fuzzphony:doctor --format=prometheus</code> prints the doctor
checks as metrics for node_exporter's textfile collector.</p>
{% endblock %}
